PART C: outside/inside lesson for n=14
========================================================================
At the initial AP witness speeds {1..13}, t=1/14:
  - outside: the 14-gon is regular and the observer is the missing clasp;
  - the two clasp-adjacent gaps are exactly 1/14, so loneliness is a
    compactified boundary source, not an open source cell;
  - inside: 78 runner-runner chords are forced from only 14 outside gaps,
    split into D_14 channels ((1, 12), (2, 12), (3, 12), (4, 12), (5, 12), (6, 12), (7, 6)), with 6 hidden diameter ties;
  - those diameter ties are precisely boundary data: a tie Hamiltonian path
    is needed before the inside tournament is a genuine simplex relation.

So the hidden inside arcs are not extra free variables.  They are
shadow data of the outside gap necklace, except on the wall where
diameter/endpoint ties create compactified choices.  This is why the
LRC proof target should be a labelled boundary/endpoint-debt statement,
not a free simplex-edge argument.

