SYNTHESIS
========================================================================
1. A tournament is a simplex relation, but circular/LRC-realizable
   tournaments are not a simplex cube: they are images of an outside
   polygon gap necklace under interval-sum threshold maps.
2. The dihedral group sees the outside polygon; its hidden inside arcs
   are chord-length channel orbits.  These channels are the right
   coordinates for regular-polygon extremals.
3. LRC marks a clasp vertex.  Source means the clasp has an empty
   forbidden arc.  The AP/regular polygon has that empty arc only on
   the closed wall; for even n it also carries hidden diameter ties.
4. For n=14, the regular-polygon wall has 6 hidden diameter ties and
   78 inside chords determined by 14 outside gaps.  The next proof
   target is to show non-AP sweeps cannot keep all outside clasp gaps
   closed while cycling the hidden boundary debt forever.
